# CASE TOOLS

Case-layer capabilities are the memory and reporting surface of the
platform. They are provided by the platform (case service, evidence
graph, audit trail), not by a domain investigator:
- case create / context / status — the case shell and its
  objective, scope, and constraints.
- evidence linking — attach evidence nodes, provenance, and
  relationships to a case.
- finding management — promote verified evidence to findings and
  track review state.
- investigation timeline — the immutable record of executed work.
- audit — tamper-evident tool activity and decisions.
- report assembly — compose the case record into a report.

These capabilities never invent conclusions. They preserve,
organize, reconcile, and present the work performed by analysts and
domain specialists.
